{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 5, :comments ["<b>וכוסי</b> — like 'my portion,' from the root of תכוסו על השה (Exodus 12:21), and similar to above: מנת כוסם (Psalms 16:5). And because it is a beverage, like כוסי רויה (Psalms 16:5) — [that derivation] is not correct." "<b>And the word תומיך</b> — like ותומך שבט (Genesis 49:10), for the consonantal arrangement is like מוציא; and to take it as a noun-pattern like מושיב is very far-fetched."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 16, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:27:21.450290659Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}